# subwave-aio bundles Icecast2, Liquidsoap, Caddy, Node controller, and Python Piper into a single container.
# The internal supervisor (docker/aio/supervisor.sh) requires root at startup to initialize runtime configs (/etc/icecast2, /var/log),
# uses sudo to drop to icecast2 user, and runs multi-service process supervision.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# Multi-process supervisor requires default capabilities (chown, setuid, setgid, net_bind_service) for Caddy and Icecast2
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106
